// 4. Style them in src/styles/creature.css. Use percentages for sizes and positions.
// 5. Share styles with a base class, then use joined classes such as
//    .ear.left and .ear.right to position matching features separately.
// 6. Make shapes at https://bennettfeely.com/clippy/ and add their clip-path CSS.
// 7. Use transform: rotate(...) to tilt features and give your character expression.
// 8. Test the pupils, check your percentage values, and explain your design choices.
